{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1538151-anyone-picked-up-crimson-gutters","id":1538151,"title":"Anyone picked up Crimson Gutters?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-05T14:31:48-07:00","id":1538151,"title":"Anyone picked up Crimson Gutters?","content":"I glanced through it and didn't see any reason to spend my hard earned money \ud83d\udcb8\ud83d\udcb0 on it and the lack of lore sheets certainly made my choice easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T14:45:11-07:00","id":1538154,"title":"","content":"i enjoyed it myself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T15:54:33-07:00","id":1538156,"title":"","content":"I picked it up myself and quite enjoyed it. It is quite clearly directed at new storytellers and new players. For experienced storytellers it probably isn't as useful. I however really enjoyed the way it presented all the rules and politics of vampire in an easily digestible way and made it make sense. When I run games for new players I'll probably steal a bit. It also Introduced the church of Caine as a sort of alternative to the cam and the anarchs which is neat.<br /> <br /> There's also some helpful charts for generating your characters sire background and why they were embraced.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T16:09:01-07:00","id":1538157,"title":"","content":"Nope, unless you are a complete newbie ST there are like dozens of better, more equipped books you can use to adapt to your chronicles and without repeating the most basics of being a Vampire while costing way less 45 bucks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T23:21:49-07:00","id":1538165,"title":"","content":"It's okay, I guess.<br /> <br /> You have this campaign which at times felt a bit too generic to me. The structure gives you one chapter as introduction and then you play a questline from one of three factions (Camarilla, Anarchs or Church of Caine). At times, it felt to me like I was reading a walkthrough of a videogame. But I guess, it depends on what you want from a book like this one.<br /> <br /> I had higher expectations for what they would do with the Church of Caine as a playable faction. At least it expands it a little bit with what you can thematically explore. Although, you used to be able to play the Sabbat for some of that stuff. And Cults of the Blood Gods offers a more in-depth look (the book is mentioned in the description of the Church of Caine as well), so it feels almost like a requirement to have that supplement if you want to play the Church of Caine questline in the book (so that you can add some extra flavor to that organization).<br /> <br /> The feeding-complications are also a neat add-on for new STs and helpful. Two things, though. First, the Predator-Types from the V5 Players Guide aren't covered. I understood the choice in Bloodstained Love where when a character's Clan was one from the Players Guide, it also offered an alternative from the corebook (in case the group didn't own the Players Guide). But a book like this one should cover the Predator Types of the Players Guide as well (and hey, maybe that's what will convince somebody to pick up that book). Of course, the issue here is the high price-point of having that expectation but that's a general problem with Renegade.<br /> <br /> The second problem with the Feeding-complications is one they listed for Siren called &quot;Dom To Sub&quot;. This is what it says: &quot;Your latest conquest is all too willing to submit to your every desire. But once they have you in bed, they swiftly click a pair of handcuffs around your wrists and secure you to the bed. They seem interested in continuing but with the tables turned. If you submit, they produce more restraints, but their proclivities (while mundane) are quite brutal, leading you to get hurt. Unlike most on the fetish scene, they don\u2019t want to accept any safe words.&quot; That is quite the thing to spring on an unexpecting player... Seriously, you need to know the people at your table <i>really </i>well before doing something like this. Maybe they should've left that one for Bloodstained Love instead rather than this introduction-chronicle-book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-06T21:08:44-07:00","id":1538192,"title":"","content":"The only thing that was sort of interesting was the pregenerated characters that you could use in different games, but it wasn't enough for me to spend the money on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}